<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Yen Tu by Motorbike: Safety Checklist | Hanoi Motorbike Guide</h1>
<p>Safety on the Yen Tu ride is not a feeling and not a product, it is a checklist that gets executed whether the morning feels dangerous or not, because the route&rsquo;s two halves punish different inattention: the corridor punishes what traffic forgets and the mountain punishes what pride pretends. This guide writes the checklist for both halves, refuses to quote conditions, distances or statistics, and hands every live question to the desk that answers them daily at 112 Nguyen Van Cu before the machine even leaves the yard.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk hands over a checked machine and an honest briefing for the northeast run before either meets the road. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, absorb the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The Checklist Habit</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The Machine Check Before The Plain</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The Body Check Before The Climb</a></li>
